    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d113-a31">

                <pb facs="0291" n="219" xml:id="pg219"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 30 in No. 331.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Barrows to Mr.
                            Lowell.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Dublin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-10-31"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 31,
                        1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith a
                    letter from United States Consular Agent Tinsley, of Limerick, relating to the
                    case of James F. Daly, recently arrested under the coercion act, and now
                    confined in Limerick jail.</p>
                <p>I inclose Daly’s naturalization papers and his letter to Mr. Tinsley, and
                    respectfully ask for instructions.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>B. H. BARROWS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
